\citation{fewshot}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Sign election in update space and in factor space are different operations.} (a) The published algorithm forms each specialist's update $\Delta _i = B_iA_i$ and elects a sign per \emph  {parameter of the update}. (b) The standard LoRA implementation, and the one we use, applies the same rule independently to the $A$ factors and to the $B$ factors and multiplies the results, so signs are elected per \emph  {factor entry}. Because each entry of $\Delta $ is a sum over the rank, no factor entry corresponds to one parameter of the update, and the two merges do not coincide: on random factors at $r{=}4$ with three specialists and density $0.5$ their outputs have cosine similarity $0.40$ and disagree in sign on $39\%$ of entries. We use (b) because the alternative --- assembling $\Delta $, merging, and re-extracting by SVD --- changes the adapter's rank and adds reconstruction error before the merging rule is evaluated.}}{7}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:factorspace}{{2}{7}{\textbf {Sign election in update space and in factor space are different operations.} (a) The published algorithm forms each specialist's update $\Delta _i = B_iA_i$ and elects a sign per \emph {parameter of the update}. (b) The standard LoRA implementation, and the one we use, applies the same rule independently to the $A$ factors and to the $B$ factors and multiplies the results, so signs are elected per \emph {factor entry}. Because each entry of $\Delta $ is a sum over the rank, no factor entry corresponds to one parameter of the update, and the two merges do not coincide: on random factors at $r{=}4$ with three specialists and density $0.5$ their outputs have cosine similarity $0.40$ and disagree in sign on $39\%$ of entries. We use (b) because the alternative --- assembling $\Delta $, merging, and re-extracting by SVD --- changes the adapter's rank and adds reconstruction error before the merging rule is evaluated}{figure.caption.5}{}}
